From ec616706f6331c9b9bbf5c2921568578605eb927 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:30:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] process dock test: spawn through an rc-free bash so
 the idle row reads "starting" under any HOME
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

test_dock_paints_processes_under_agents_and_retires_finished_rows failed on every run of
post-merge check t_01a1d6672d341a89 on hermes-worker-5 (run1, run2 and run_tests' retries).
The card blamed load, but load does not cause it. That sweep ran `env -i HOME=<empty dir> ... run_tests.sh`.
spawn_local starts jobs as `$SHELL -lic`. Without ~/.sudo_as_admin_successful or ~/.hushlogin,
Ubuntu's /etc/bash.bashrc prints its sudo hint, which becomes the job's first output. The
registry strips only bash's job-control warnings, so the idle `sleep 30` row painted

    ⚙ sleep 30 · 0s · last: See "man sudo_root" for details.

instead of `starting`.

Repro (worker-6, load 7.7): the sweep's exact env -i/empty-HOME invocation fails 3/3 attempts.
The same tree passes under the real HOME on worker-5 at load 33 and on worker-6 at load 60.

Fix (test-only): `_quiet_shell` pins spawn_local's login-shell seam (`bg_login_argv`) to
`bash --noprofile --norc -c`, so the host's rc files never decide what the dock shows. The
dock is under test here, not the rc files. The `starting` assertion now prints the dock text on
failure.

Verified:
- GREEN under the sweep's empty HOME at load 6.7 and again at load 36.
- GREEN under the real HOME at load 50 (16 cores).
- Mutant M-dock (cli_process_dock.process_activity: `t("cli.dock.starting")` -> `""`) is
  killed by this test.

The other test on the card, test_refusal_records_the_streak_and_names_the_record, was already
made hermetic on main by 00eaacb397ce (pins os.getloadavg/effective_cores through _host_load).
No change is needed here. Without that pin it fails at load 52 (`worker_load_pressure`). With
the pin it passes at load 36-50, and mutant M-alarm (`"record": record_for(exc)` -> `None`) is
killed by it.

Card: t_01a1d6822cd87a47
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_process_dock.py | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_process_dock.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_process_dock.py
index 6a632a5558..d96d640f79 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_process_dock.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_process_dock.py
@@ -14,12 +14,25 @@ def _wait(predicate, timeout=5.0):
         time.sleep(0.05)
 
 
+def _quiet_shell(monkeypatch):
+    """Spawn through bash without rc files. ``spawn_local`` runs ``$SHELL -lic``, so the host's startup output
+    becomes a job's first output: under an empty HOME (no ``~/.sudo_as_admin_successful``) Ubuntu's
+    /etc/bash.bashrc prints its sudo hint and the idle row read ``last: See "man sudo_root" for details.``
+    instead of ``starting`` (t_01a1d6822cd87a47). The dock, not the host's rc files, is under test here."""
+    import tools.process_registry as process_registry_module
+    from tools.environments.local import _find_bash
+
+    monkeypatch.setattr(process_registry_module, 'bg_login_argv',
+                        lambda command: [_find_bash(), '--noprofile', '--norc', '-c', command])
+
+
 def test_dock_paints_processes_under_agents_and_retires_finished_rows(monkeypatch):
     from hermes_cli import cli_process_dock
     from hermes_cli.cli_subagent_monitor import SubagentMonitor
     from tools import delegate_tool_registry as registry
     from tools.process_registry import process_registry
 
+    _quiet_shell(monkeypatch)
     monkeypatch.setattr(registry, '_active_subagents', {})
     owner = SimpleNamespace(session_id='owner')
     registry._register_subagent(dict(subagent_id='a1', owner_agent_session_id='owner',
@@ -40,7 +53,7 @@ def test_dock_paints_processes_under_agents_and_retires_finished_rows(monkeypatc
         procs_at = next(i for i, line in enumerate(lines)
                         if t('cli.subagents.processes_heading', summary=summary, controls='') in line)
         assert agents_at < procs_at
-        assert any('⚙ sleep 30' in line and t('cli.dock.starting') in line for line in lines)
+        assert any('⚙ sleep 30' in line and t('cli.dock.starting') in line for line in lines), text
         assert any(f"✘ echo hello-dock; exit 3 · {t('cli.dock.exit_code', code=3)}" in line for line in lines)
         assert all(get_cwidth(line) <= 100 for line in lines)
         # Every viewport keeps at least one row of each block.
